1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kilde: Nermo.org
2 CONT
2 CONT RESIDENCE: 1645, Betalte koppskatt (Bergensborger 1599-?) 
2 CONT
2 CONT OCCUPATION: Rådmann i Bergen (innsatt 21 Juli 1617)
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH: ABT 1570, (f gr.sk Crometij/Cromartie, Skottland?) 
2 CONT
2 CONT BAPTISM: (innv. fra Walls, Orkney (=Cromarty) ?) 
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH: 28 Aug 1647, Bergen, HO 
2 CONT
2 CONT BURIAL: (Borgerskap i Bergen 1607/9 ?) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Cromartie was a merchant burgess of Bergen from 1599. His father [SSNE 6887] had also been a burgess of the town. Thomas served as a town councillor from 1617. Thomas formed part of an Orcadian community in the town as his 
2 CONC neighbours were James Anderson Dishingtun [SSNE 5200] and Thomas Quoybanks [SSNE 4507] who both witnessed his sale of land. In addition, Cromartie's cousin William [SSNE 6889] was also in Bergen. Thomas had a house and warehouses 
2 CONC at the harbour (on the southwest of Bergen's Vaag) which were later inherited by his son, Daniel. He signed a disposition in 1640 to William Stewart of Mains, of a farthing udal land in Kirk, South Ronaldsay, Orkney with sasine. T
2 CONC homas died in 1647. His grandson, Thomas Danielsen, was a sailmaker and merchant and his probate records are substantial. .......................................................................... National Archives of Scotland GD 
2 CONC 195/49-50. Thanks to Lars Maersk Hansen for further details on Cromartie.  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Rådmann i Bergen i 21. juli 1617.
