2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT About Dominicus Berntsen Nagel Ifølge boka "Bergens prester" og rettelser i "Bergen Stift" var Dominicus Nagel født i Bergen 11. mars 1700, døpt 14. mars 1700. Hans foreldre var Bernt Dominicussen Nagel og Karen Andersdatter Hauri
2 CONC tz. Han var gift med Cathrine Grønbech død 1790 på Smedsvig i Ryfylke, datter av Christen Grønbech, sogneprest til Askvoll. Familien flyttet til Førde etter den store bybrannen i Bergen i 1702, da Dominikus var 2 år.
2 CONT
2 CONT Studied theology in Copenhagen from 1719 to 1723 and completed Embetseksamen with top marks at age 22. Assistant chaplain in Brønnøysund for five years. On 4 July 1729 appointed vicar at Biri near Gjøvik. Transferred to Skjold aro
2 CONC und 1733 and in 1740 was appointed 'Prost' (Rector in charge of several parishes) in Ryfylke. He was involved in several scandals and court cases due to his violent behaviour, but is also credited with having established the area'
2 CONC s Lepers hospital and advancing the school system. He was removed from his position by the King of Denmark in 1749, but died before this royal decree reached him.
