1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The name of Daniel Cromerty's wife is not in any records, but has been derived from the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT In this Bergen family (as for many others) the following rules for naming children were followed)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st son- paternal grandfather's name
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd son-maternal grandfather's name
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd son- great gr father's name
2 CONT
2 CONT or names from uncles
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st daughter- paternal grandmother's name
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd daughter-maternal grandmother's name
2 CONT
2 CONT etc
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniels sons were: Thomas, Berendt, Ludvig, Jan
2 CONT
2 CONT daughters: Emmiche, Wibeche, Trinche
2 CONT
2 CONT Berendt and Ludvig were the main Names in the Middelstorp family. From this is derived that Daniels wife was a Middelstorp. Furthermore Thomas D Cromerty and the Middeltorps were partners in a burial site beneath Nykirken in Berge
2 CONC n
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel's eldest Son Thomas thus named his first son Daniel, 2nd Hendrich and his first daughter Ael (Ahl, Alida), 2nd Giertrud. From this is derived that Thomas Mother's name was Ael
