3 CITY Cape Town
3 STAE WC
3 CTRY South Africa
1 OCCU Shopkeeper (Shop was located at 138 Long street Cape Town)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was born in Denmark in a village called Skamstrup some 60 kilometres west of Copenhagen in 1777. <br/>
2 CONT His youngest brother was born in 'Skamstrup Præstegaard', the house of the preast in the town, so his father was a priest. The youngest brother seems to be the only child besides Jacob to travel as he died in London, England. <br/
2 CONC >
2 CONT Jacob married in Cape Town 9/2 1806 and 2½ month later their first child was born.<br/>
2 CONT So he must have arrived to Cape Town from Denmark before 1805, probably som time before.<br/>
2 CONT He had a shop in Cape Town, but what kind of shop is not known (yet).
