1 NOTE {geni:about_me} An Alexander Cunningham and his father William Cunningham are in a letter (1700) dated January 26 1565/66 (under the great seal of Scotland) given land in West-Barnis and Gallowsyde " in constabularia de Craill, vi
2 CONC c, Fyffe" Signed by Mary Stuart and Henry her husband "Rex et Regina". Part of same land is given to John Cunningham "filio legitimo Willelmi C. de Barnis in another letter (2038) dated April 10 1572. We can also learn here that W
2 CONC illiams wife was Beatrix Lawmont. Source: "The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland" Volume IV A.D. 1546-1580.
2 CONT
2 CONT Scotish Laird John Cunningham of Crail, Fife in Scotland filed official papers, 16 April 1596 in Edinburgh, to"recognize" John "Hans Kønig" Cunningham, 1575 as his son.
2 CONT
